#97's fix is committed and queued with the manager, but it has not landed yet. After 3h20m in the queue (from 08:22Z) there is still no verdict, and the run hits its time limit now. The manager will land it after the run and post its verdict on the issue. The next run then posts the outcome comment and closes #97.

**What's queued on `looper/looper-97`:**
- **842d5ed, the fix:** an author GitHub reports as `CONTRIBUTOR` or `NONE` now directs a run if their permission on the repository is `write`, `maintain` or `admin`, the same check a `COLLABORATOR` already got.
  - Each author is looked up once per prompt, and a failed lookup is not cached and leaves the text as data.
  - The tests cover all five cases the issue asks for: CONTRIBUTOR with admin directs; CONTRIBUTOR with read, NONE, a failed lookup and the injected comment all stay data.
  - README.md and STATE.md are updated to match.
- **09316ea, why the previous land went red:**
  - `tests/forge.test.sh` failed in the manager's gate job because `LOOPER_REPORT_APP_ID` was set there, which made looper-dispatch try to get an App token.
  - The repo-looper, looper-dispatch and tacplus tests broke the same way inside a looper job.
  - Each of the four tests now clears the `LOOPER_*`, `CI_*`, `GH_*`, `GITHUB_*` and `GITLAB_*` variables it inherits.
  - Since this fixes what the previous run had written up as a proposal, I removed that note from PROPOSALS.md.

**Checks:**
- All 18 gates in gates.yaml's full set pass in this job's own environment. The four changed tests were re-run after the change; the other 14 were run on this same code just before it (their files didn't change).
- `looper-trace check` passes: no handlers touched.
- The report App's token can already read collaborator permissions: it returns `admin` for jodydadescott on tacplus and looper. It needs no new GitHub permission.

**tacplus#315:** there was nothing to requeue. It had already been picked up again (`looper:in-progress`), and Jody has since marked it `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#106`. I left its labels alone.

The last checkpoint on the branch records all of this for the next run.
